# Question generation protocol

Before creating or changing questions, read
`docs/question-generation-protocol.md` and use `content/question-template.md`.

- Use a PDF or other reference only to map skills, difficulty, and variety;
  never reproduce or closely paraphrase protected exercises or solutions.
- Plan coverage by subject, topic, subtopic, difficulty, and command type
  before drafting a batch.
- Every item must be original, multiple choice with four distinct options and
  one verified answer, three progressive hints, plausible distractors, and a
  self-contained commented solution.
- Write every mathematical expression as valid `$...$`; never use `$$`.
- Run the protocol audit before creating a migration. Do not publish or import
  content that fails provenance, answer, formatting, diversity, or taxonomy
  checks.
